Subject: [PATCH] Answer a failed fetch with a network error

When the worker's own fetch fails (offline, a script an ad blocker
refuses, a navigation the reader cut short), upstream logs the error
and resolves respondWith with undefined. The browser then throws
"Failed to convert value to 'Response'", uncaught, so one failed
request is two red lines in the console, neither of which says much.

Response.error() is the network error the page would have seen with
no worker in between, and nothing is thrown.

---
--- a/coi-serviceworker.js
+++ b/coi-serviceworker.js
@@ -65,7 +65,12 @@
                         headers: newHeaders,
                     });
                 })
-                .catch((e) => console.error(e))
+                // A fetch that fails (offline, a blocked script, a
+                // navigation cut short) is a network error for the page,
+                // as it would be with no worker. Logging it and answering
+                // undefined made it two console errors, the second an
+                // uncaught "Failed to convert value to 'Response'".
+                .catch(() => Response.error())
         );
     });
 
